findings.recommendation:
From min-width 1800px, put the open check in a sticky side column beside the viewer. analysis-1's CSS as written is broken: on a checkpoint with no chips (FLUX) it put the panel below the viewer's row (panel at y=1011, Ask the critic at y=1413, off-screen). Use this version instead, verified by injection on FLUX and Animagine at both viewports (S = .stage:has(> #tag-validation-wide > #prompt-analysis:not([hidden]))):
@media (min-width:1800px){ S{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) clamp(520px,30vw,760px);grid-template-rows:auto auto 1fr;column-gap:18px;row-gap:18px;align-items:start} S>*{grid-column:1/-1} S #tag-validation{grid-column:1;grid-row:1} S #prompt-analysis{grid-column:2;grid-row:1/span 3;position:sticky;top:68px;max-height:calc(100vh - 86px);overflow-y:auto} S>#viewer{grid-column:1;grid-row:2} S>#viewer-note{grid-column:1;grid-row:3} S>.gallery-head{grid-row:4} S>#gallery{grid-row:5} S>#sheet{grid-row:6} S>#btn-more{grid-row:7} }
Two parts are load-bearing. The explicit rows stop the gallery from auto-placing into an empty chip row. The '1fr' last row takes the panel's extra height below the viewer instead of above it; without it the viewer was pushed to y=343. Result: the image stays at y=109, fully visible after Check and after the critic answers, at both viewports. The panel sticks at top 68 with its own scroll. Below 1800 px leave the stacking as it is, optionally capped at max-height:55vh; overflow-y:auto.

