directions.thesis:
At QHD the page is a 330 px form (12.9% of 2560) over a long scrolling document. The image just made sits in a box with empty space on both sides, and the gallery starts at y=1105, so 200 px of it is visible. The Refine dialog is 460 px wide and shows its source as a 72 px thumbnail. The workbench turns the page into a fixed 100vh workspace of three columns that each scroll on their own:
- a sectioned control column (435 px) with Generate always pinned at its foot;
- a canvas (1523 px) that is always the image you are working on: the newest result, the image you picked, a pass beside its source, the source of a Refine with the crop it will keep, or the contact sheet;
- a rail (538 px) with an inspector for the selected image over a 4-column library.

Refine stops being a modal. It becomes the inspector's panel for the selected image, and the canvas shows that image at 1:1 next to its controls. The prototype runs on the real page, with the real scripts and the fake server. Generate (Ctrl+Enter), a batch of 4, a docked Refine run, the lightbox, the sheet and the prompt check all still work with it applied.

